**PETITION FOR SOLE ASSIGNMENT OF THE BEACON KEY**

---

*Submitted to the Centennial Allocation Assembly, Ship-Year 412, Cycle 247*

*By Miranda Chen-Okonkwo-Voss, Proprietor of Feed Designation MCV-7 ("The Between")*

---

**WHEREAS** the Founders' Charter of Ship-Year 8 established the Beacon as the unified consciousness of all settlers aboard Long Miranda, to be administered jointly by the Founders' Circle as trustees of the collective wake-cycle;

**WHEREAS** the Centennial Allocation provision of said Charter, dormant these four generations, now opens all chartered instruments to reassignment by demonstrated capacity to serve the common welfare;

**WHEREAS** the Beacon key, held in fragmented stewardship by twelve descendants of the first crew, has become a mechanism of factional compromise rather than unified voice—its programming the product of twelve retinal visions, twelve wake-anxieties, twelve inherited grievances played out in the single minute every settler sees before the self selects its day;

**WHEREAS** my channel, MCV-7, reaches 94.7% of active retinal feeds per cycle, with mean engagement duration of 847 seconds—metrics exceeding every other discretionary feed, and second only to the Beacon itself in total ship-wide exposure;

**WHEREAS** this reach was built without charter privilege, without wake-cycle mandate, without the compulsion of a captive audience rising from dream;

**WHEREAS** the Founders' Circle, in their most recent joint programming cycle, devoted 34% of Beacon content to internal disputes of lineage and precedence, 28% to warnings of external threat without actionable intelligence, and 22% to ceremonial acknowledgment of their own continuity—leaving 16% for the actual business of ship-life, crew morale, and the psychic maintenance of four generations' remove from any planetary horizon;

**WHEREAS** a single vision, proven in open competition for voluntary attention, would restore to the Beacon its original purpose: not the preservation of a caste, but the orientation of a collective toward shared survival and meaning;

---

**I PETITION THE ASSEMBLY** to assign the Beacon key to sole stewardship, under the following constraints I voluntarily accept:

**First**—That the Beacon remain non-commercial, its content distinct from MCV-7 programming, its purpose the common wake rather than private gain;

**Second**—That I submit to recall by supermajority of the Assembly if any cycle's Beacon content draws sustained negative engagement exceeding 15% of active feeds;

**Third**—That I train three successors from outside the Founders' lineages, to be confirmed by Assembly vote, ensuring no reconsolidation of hereditary control;

**Fourth**—That the minute of the wake-cycle remain inviolate—no extension, no subdivision, no purchase of adjacent seconds;

**Fifth**—That the Founders' Circle retain ceremonial recognition in the ship's record, and access to archival Beacon content for historical study, though not for programming input.

---

The Founders built Long Miranda to outlast their own memory. The Circle clings to a key that was never meant to be a birthright, only a responsibility. I do not ask for inheritance. I ask for the work.

The settlers already choose where their attention lingers. Let the Assembly recognize what they have chosen.

---

*Miranda Chen-Okonkwo-Voss*
*Witnessed this cycle by retinal signature*

